        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Verify signed marketplace feed refresh",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Wire signed marketplace feed profiles into hosted catalog refresh using the signed envelope verifier and configured threshold.\n- Persist bounded signed-feed trust state with hosted snapshots, and re-verify signed snapshots with the current source profile before using them.\n- Count signed-feed thresholds over unique normalized Ed25519 public-key material so duplicate key IDs or duplicate key material cannot weaken a multi-signature threshold.\n- Keep signed profiles fail-closed on invalid live bodies or unsigned old snapshots, without changing install eligibility or the existing marketplace refresh/entries payload shape.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/config/zod-schema.marketplaces.test.ts src/plugins/official-external-plugin-catalog-envelope.test.ts src/plugins/official-external-plugin-catalog.test.ts`\n- `pnpm exec oxlint --deny-warnings src/plugins/official-external-plugin-catalog-envelope.ts src/plugins/official-external-plugin-catalog-envelope.test.ts src/config/zod-schema.ts src/config/zod-schema.marketplaces.test.ts`\n- `pnpm exec oxfmt --check src/plugins/official-external-plugin-catalog-envelope.ts src/plugins/official-external-plugin-catalog-envelope.test.ts src/config/zod-schema.ts src/config/zod-schema.marketplaces.test.ts`\n- `pnpm tsgo:core`\n- `pnpm db:kysely:check`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `codex review --base fork/feeds-trust-source-profiles` - clean after verifier hardening\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nSource harness from this branch generated an Ed25519 key, signed a hosted catalog feed envelope, loaded it through a signed feed profile, verified persisted snapshot trust state, then attempted offline fallback from an unsigned old snapshot under the same signed profile.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"acceptedSource\": \"hosted\",\n  \"acceptedEntries\": [\n    \"@openclaw/signed-proof\"\n  ],\n  \"acceptedTrust\": {\n    \"mode\": \"signed\",\n    \"signedBy\": \"proof-root\",\n    \"signatureCount\": 1,\n    \"threshold\": 1,\n    \"verifiedAt\": \"2026-07-01T00:00:01.000Z\"\n  },\n  \"snapshotTrust\": {\n    \"mode\": \"signed\",\n    \"signedBy\": \"proof-root\",\n    \"signatureCount\": 1,\n    \"threshold\": 1,\n    \"verifiedAt\": \"2026-07-01T00:00:01.000Z\"\n  },\n  \"unsignedSnapshotRejected\": true,\n  \"unsignedSnapshotError\": \"hosted catalog feed offline mode; snapshot fallback failed: hosted catalog signed envelope is malformed\"\n}\n```\n\nAdditional ClawSweeper fix proof:\nThe config schema rejects malformed raw base64url signing keys, duplicate signed-feed key IDs, and duplicate normalized public keys. The envelope verifier also counts threshold satisfaction over unique normalized public-key material, with regression coverage proving two key IDs backed by the same public key cannot satisfy `threshold: 2`.\n\n## Stack notes\n\nThis is OpenClaw trust series PR #4 / OpenClaw PR #3, stacked after:\n\n- #98299 signed hosted feed envelope verifier primitives\n- #98316 source-profile trust config at `16cbe678ce`\n\nThe PR currently targets `main` as a draft because the dependency branches are on the fork. Reviewers should focus on the top commit `3ce0cfafaf` until the earlier trust PRs land.\r\n",
